WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.282
The results are strong on both tasks.

00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:07.071
For the Gaussian example, the loss function peaks
exactly at the true mean,

00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:10.135
confirming the method recovers the right answer,

00:00:10.215 --> 00:00:13.710
and the discriminator converges within about ten epochs.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:18.818
For the jet width, the team unfolds the first and
second moments simultaneously.

00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:25.777
Scanning the loss as a function of each candidate
moment produces curves whose peaks land on the true values,

00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:30.119
with a mean absolute error of two hundredths of a
percent or better.

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:34.460
That is sub-percent agreement between the unfolded
and true moments.
